# Options for the dashboard service. After editing:
#   sudo systemctl restart sailingdashboard
#
# Source:  --can can0   (SH-C30A with candleLight/gs_usb firmware, the usual case)
#          --slcan /dev/ttyACM0   (if the adapter has slcan firmware instead)
# IMU:     --imu /dev/serial0     BNO085 heel/pitch (used only if no attitude sensor is on the bus)
#          --imu-invert-roll --imu-invert-pitch   if the IMU's heel or pitch is reversed
# Logging: the bus is recorded to /var/lib/sailingdashboard/recordings (Logs button on the tablet).
#          --record-max-gb 4   keep at most 4 GB of recordings (default 8; oldest deleted first)
#          --no-record         turn recording off
# Weather: --weather-home casco   area to fetch weather for before GPS has a position
#          (casco, boston or LAT,LON); after that it follows the boat
# Tuning:  --variation -14.3   only needed if no device on the bus sends variation
#          --invert-roll       if heel shows on the wrong side
#          --heading-offset 2  if heading reads 2 degrees low
DASH_ARGS="--can can0 --port 80"
